<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rodolfo Graziani</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1882–1955</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rodolfo Graziani was an Italian general who directed the brutal reconquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/libya">Libya</a>, deporting the nomads of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyrenaica">Cyrenaica</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/concentration-camp">concentration camps</a>. He commanded on the southern front in the invasion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a> and became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroy-of-india">viceroy</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italian-east-africa">Italian East Africa</a>, where an attempt on his life in 1937 was followed by mass killings in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/addis-ababa">Addis Ababa</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rodolfo-graziani.jpg" alt="Rodolfo Graziani" width="320" height="453" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Marshal_Rodolfo_Graziani_potrait.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
